<h2>Practical read-only diagnostic handoff checklist</h2>
<ol>
<li>Identify the exact car, engine, production range and installed system before choosing the diagnostic application.</li>
<li>Check the interface and software developer's documented support for the vehicle and target module.</li>
<li>Preserve the original symptom, warning lamps and electrical state before clearing diagnostic memory.</li>
<li>Confirm the tool's recognized VIN, responding modules and any missing communication links.</li>
<li>Read and save faults, freeze-frame/context data and safe live values where supported.</li>
<li>Correlate symptoms and the module's observations with independent mechanical or electrical evidence.</li>
<li>Separate a confirmed condition from the hypothesis that a particular component caused it.</li>
<li>Stop before any coding, actuator command, service reset or programming unless authorized procedure and safety prerequisites have been established.</li>
</ol>